module med-criminal-local-rules.local-rules

import core.authority.{ CaseOrder }
import core.frcrimp45.{ frcrimp45 }
import frcrimp.deadlines.{ VerdictOrDischarge }

// The District of Maine's own criminal periods. The criminal local rules
// start with Local Rule 101 and each corresponds to the Federal Rule of
// Criminal Procedure of the same number less 100; rules that apply to
// both civil and criminal matters are Local Rules 1 to 83 (D. Me. Local
// R. 1(b)), whose periods are lit/med's. FRCrimP 45 computes every period
// the Local Rules state (D. Me. Local R. 145). No trigger carries a
// service method: FRCrimP 45(c)'s three added days follow the manner of
// service, which is not modeled here. The Court may modify the rules when
// justice so requires (D. Me. Local R. 1(c)).
//
// Periods that are FRCrimP periods stay in lit/frcrimp and are only named
// here: objections to the initial presentence report are filed within 14
// days after its disclosure (D. Me. Local R. 132(a); FRCrimP 32(f)(1)),
// and the report is deemed disclosed when filed on ECF (D. Me. Local R.
// 132(f)(2)). The 14-day objection period may be shortened only with the
// defendant's consent; the Court may modify the other Rule 132 times for
// good cause (D. Me. Local R. 132(e)).
//
// Conditions that are not deadlines from an event stay in notes: a trial
// date is ordinarily set at the arraignment (Local Rule 110, whose
// heading the vendored sectioning leaves unmarked); a final pretrial
// conference may be held under FRCrimP 17.1 (D. Me. Local R. 117);
// opening statements may not exceed 30 minutes except by leave of Court
// (D. Me. Local R. 123(a)); a criminal jury is 12 members (D. Me. Local
// R. 124.2(a)), and the order of the government's 6 and the defendants'
// 10 peremptory challenges is set out in D. Me. Local R. 124.2(d)(2);
// further jury instruction requests may be made at the close of the
// evidence when their need could not reasonably have been foreseen (D.
// Me. Local R. 130); objections to the revocation report are heard orally
// at the revocation hearing (D. Me. Local R. 132.1(b)); motions are
// decided without oral argument unless the Court orders otherwise (D. Me.
// Local R. 147(e)); the deemed waiver of an unopposed motion does not
// apply to motions filed during trial (D. Me. Local R. 147(b)(2)); a
// defense attorney continues until relieved by this Court or the Court
// of Appeals, and after a notice of appeal a motion to withdraw goes to
// the Court of Appeals (D. Me. Local R. 157.5(b)). Petty offenses follow
// D. Me. Local R. 158, and sealing D. Me. Local R. 157.6.
//
// The earlier D. Me. criminal outline's FRCrimP flow and its decisions
// (United States v. Salerno, Brady v. Maryland, Barker v. Wingo, Zedner
// v. United States, Boykin v. Alabama, Missouri v. Frye, Jackson v.
// Virginia, United States v. Booker, Roe v. Flores-Ortega, Garza v.
// Idaho) are FRCrimP, Speedy Trial Act or constitutional authority and
// belong to lit/frcrimp; they are removed here: no reporter text is
// vendored.
/// A memorandum of law in support of or in opposition to a dispositive
/// motion or a motion to suppress evidence: at most 20 pages except by
/// prior leave of Court (D. Me. Local R. 147(d)).
limit dispositive-memorandum {
  pages <= 20 cite "D. Me. Local R. 147(d)"
} cite "D. Me. Local R. 147(d)"

/// A memorandum in support of or in opposition to any other motion: at
/// most 10 pages (D. Me. Local R. 147(d)).
limit motion-memorandum { pages <= 10 cite "D. Me. Local R. 147(d)" } cite "D. Me. Local R. 147(d)"
/// A reply memorandum: at most 7 pages, strictly confined to new matter
/// raised in the objection (D. Me. Local R. 147(c)).
limit reply-memorandum { pages <= 7 cite "D. Me. Local R. 147(c)" } cite "D. Me. Local R. 147(c)"
/// A trial brief: at most 20 pages except by prior leave of Court (D. Me.
/// Local R. 157.2).
limit trial-brief { pages <= 20 cite "D. Me. Local R. 157.2" } cite "D. Me. Local R. 157.2"

/// A motion, incorporating its memorandum of law, is filed (D. Me. Local
/// R. 147(a)).
event MotionFiled() paper motion-memorandum
/// A dispositive motion or a motion to suppress evidence is filed (D. Me.
/// Local R. 147(a), (d)).
event DispositiveMotionFiled() paper dispositive-memorandum
/// A written objection to a motion is filed (D. Me. Local R. 147(b)).
event ObjectionFiled() paper motion-memorandum
/// A reply memorandum is filed (D. Me. Local R. 147(c)).
event ReplyFiled() paper reply-memorandum
/// A change of plea is scheduled (D. Me. Local R. 111).
event ChangeOfPleaScheduled()
/// Jury empanelment is scheduled (D. Me. Local R. 124.1, 130).
event EmpanelmentScheduled()
/// The date set for trial (D. Me. Local R. 157.2).
event TrialScheduled()
/// A trial brief is served and filed (D. Me. Local R. 157.2).
event TrialBriefFiled() paper trial-brief
/// The sentencing hearing is scheduled (D. Me. Local R. 132(g)); the
/// FRCrimP date the presentence report counts back from is lit/frcrimp's
/// SentencingScheduled.
event SentencingHearingScheduled()
/// A finding or waiver of probable cause that a violation of supervised
/// release or probation was committed, for an arrested defendant, or the
/// initial appearance of a summonsed defendant (D. Me. Local R. 132.1(a)).
event RevocationTrigger()
/// The final determination of the action by this or any appellate court
/// (D. Me. Local R. 123(f)(2)).
event FinalDetermination()

/// D. Me. Local R. 111: counsel files any plea agreement with the Clerk at
/// least 2 business days before a scheduled change of plea.
deadline plea-agreement-filing: 2.business_days before ChangeOfPleaScheduled() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "D. Me. Local R. 111"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// D. Me. Local R. 124.1: proposed questions for jury voir dire are served
/// and submitted at least 3 days before jury empanelment.
deadline voir-dire-questions: 3.days before EmpanelmentScheduled() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "D. Me. Local R. 124.1"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// D. Me. Local R. 130: written requests for jury instructions under
/// FRCrimP 30 are served and submitted at least 3 days before jury
/// empanelment.
deadline jury-instruction-requests: 3.days before EmpanelmentScheduled() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "D. Me. Local R. 130"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// D. Me. Local R. 157.2: unless the Court orders otherwise, each party
/// serves and files a trial brief at least 3 days before the date set for
/// trial.
deadline trial-brief-filing: 3.days before TrialScheduled() counted_by frcrimp45 delegable {
  to CaseOrder
  op set
} cite "D. Me. Local R. 157.2"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// D. Me. Local R. 132(b): the probation officer files the revised
/// presentence report, with its addendum of objections and the officer's
/// comments, no more than 77 days after the verdict or finding of guilt.
/// The Court may modify the time for good cause (Local R. 132(e)).
deadline revised-psr-filing: 77.days after VerdictOrDischarge(Verdict) counted_by frcrimp45 delegable {
  to CaseOrder
  op set
} cite "D. Me. Local R. 132(b); D. Me. Local R. 132(e)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// D. Me. Local R. 132(g)(1): unless the assigned judge orders otherwise,
/// a motion for a cooperation departure or variance is filed sealed 5
/// business days before the sentencing hearing; supporting documents go
/// to the Probation Office for the judge on the same day (Local R.
/// 132(g)(2)).
deadline cooperation-motion: 5.business_days before SentencingHearingScheduled() counted_by frcrimp45 delegable {
  to CaseOrder
  op set
} cite "D. Me. Local R. 132(g)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// D. Me. Local R. 132(g)(3): unless the assigned judge orders otherwise,
/// courtesy copies of sentencing exhibits are submitted 5 business days
/// before the sentencing hearing.
deadline sentencing-exhibits: 5.business_days before SentencingHearingScheduled() counted_by frcrimp45 delegable {
  to CaseOrder
  op set
} cite "D. Me. Local R. 132(g)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// D. Me. Local R. 132.1(a): unless the Court orders otherwise, the
/// probation officer files the revocation report not more than 10
/// calendar days after the finding or waiver of probable cause, or the
/// summonsed defendant's initial appearance.
deadline revocation-report: 10.days after RevocationTrigger() counted_by frcrimp45 delegable {
  to CaseOrder
  op set
} cite "D. Me. Local R. 132.1(a)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// D. Me. Local R. 147(b)(1): unless the opposing party files a written
/// objection, with a memorandum of law, within 21 days after the filing of
/// a motion, it is deemed to have waived objection.
deadline objection-period: 21.days after MotionFiled() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "D. Me. Local R. 147(b)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// D. Me. Local R. 147(b)(1): the same 21 days for a dispositive motion or
/// a motion to suppress evidence.
deadline dispositive-objection-period: 21.days after DispositiveMotionFiled() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "D. Me. Local R. 147(b)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// D. Me. Local R. 147(c): within 14 days of the filing of an objection,
/// the moving party may file a reply memorandum.
deadline reply-period: 14.days after ObjectionFiled() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "D. Me. Local R. 147(c)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// D. Me. Local R. 123(f)(2): documentary exhibits are withdrawn by the
/// counsel who offered them within 30 days after the final determination
/// of the action by this or any appellate court; after notice the Clerk
/// may dispose of them.
deadline exhibit-withdrawal: 30.days after FinalDetermination() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "D. Me. Local R. 123(f)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}
